/-! Manuscript `thm:mc-counts`, `lem:mb-counts`, and `thm:mb-capture`
with common centers and closed radial intervals. Mixed and arbitrary-amplitude
pure branches retain their tail-equals-one normalization, logarithmic center,
all-dimension count bound, joint existence/maximum limit, and capture for all
sufficiently small fixed band widths. The three printed retained-count
probability bounds share the same normalized center and radial interval.

Items `thm:main-initial` and `cor:cp-information` are also completed at one
exponent, using the actual finite-dimensional spherical-field image, whose
Borel sigma-algebra is generated by evaluations. The capture and main
endpoints use exactly the five existing explicit literature interfaces.
Counts and the deterministic transports require no literature hypotheses.

The private capture assembly retains the first-moment record through the
existing common-witness construction, rather than discarding its normalized
center when the fixed-window reduction is applied. -/

@[expose] public section
noncomputable section

